INSTALL
=======

The plugin requires GIMP 3.0 or newer. For GIMP 2.x use version 0.4.

Building needs meson, ninja, a C compiler, gettext and the GIMP development
files (the package is called libgimp-3.0-dev on Debian and Ubuntu,
gimp-devel on Fedora).

System wide installation:

	meson setup build
	ninja -C build
	sudo ninja -C build install

User installation, into the plug-ins folder of your GIMP profile (see
Edit->Preferences->Folders->Plug-ins in GIMP for the exact path):

	meson setup build -Dplugindir=$HOME/.config/GIMP/3.2/plug-ins
	ninja -C build install

Restart GIMP after installing.

Flatpak GIMP
------------
The Flatpak version of GIMP reads user plug-ins from ~/.config/GIMP/3.2 as
well. The plugin has to be built against the GIMP of the Flatpak, using the
GNOME SDK that GIMP was built with (see "flatpak info org.gimp.GIMP"):

	flatpak install --user flathub org.gnome.Sdk//50
	flatpak run --devel --filesystem=$PWD --filesystem=~/.config/GIMP \
	  --env=PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/app/lib/pkgconfig --command=sh org.gimp.GIMP -c \
	  'meson setup build -Dplugindir=$HOME/.config/GIMP/3.2/plug-ins &&
	   ninja -C build install'

Tests
-----
tests/run.sh builds the plugin into tests/output and runs its tests in GIMP
without a window, with a throwaway GIMP profile in tests/output, so the
installed plugins and settings are not touched. It needs meson, ninja and
gimp-console of GIMP 3 (set GIMP_CONSOLE=gimp-console-3.2 if it has another
name); with gimp-plugin-devtools from https://github.com/sandbranch next to
this folder it uses the Flatpak GIMP. For a build with AddressSanitizer and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer:

	tests/run.sh -Db_sanitize=address,undefined
